    {
      "path": "/api/auth/register",
      "status": "retired",
      "documented": false,
      "reason": "Retired 2026-10-07 (#1376). The legacy credentials signup: it created a User AND a Tenant in one call and recorded no terms acceptance, so it was the second of three self-signup doors and the weaker one. Replaced by the three-step path the wizard uses — POST /api/auth/register/start (unverified user + emailed code, and the only place consent is captured), POST /api/auth/register/verify (proves the address and signs in), POST /api/me/farms (creates the farm). The login page's in-page register form went with it and now links to /start, conditional on social.farm-registration. Its real-DB rollback proof was PORTED, not deleted: tests/integration/tenant-creation-atomicity.test.ts now proves the same property against createTenantWithOwner, which is where the transaction lives on the new path. No client called it — iOS confirmed it calls five auth routes and this is not among them (agri-saas#1371)."
    },
